xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Persist HA persistent-NAT clear generations and peer replay floors so
    delayed idle-lease batches cannot restore mappings after an operator clear
    or daemon/helper restart; reclaim expired allocator clear fences (#11486).
  * Throttle REST guesses across claimed Basic usernames and IPv6 /64 source
    prefixes, and use bcrypt cost 12 for new API-auth verifiers (#11492).
  * Apply shared PAM faillock on the supported non-appliance SSH stack while
    preserving the appliance posture and administrator-owned PAM stacks
    (#11492).
  * Require a live VRF link type for tunnel bind, claim observation, and
    claim-lapse unbind; derive NAT egress diagnostics from quarantine-safe
    routing-instance ownership (#11494).
  * Require authenticated tokens for fabric state changes during dual-accept
    rollout grace while preserving grace for read-only peer RPCs (#11487).
  * Reject zone references to absent logical units and keep flow-sampling
    restrictions fail-closed rather than widening exports (#11433).
  * Retain DHCPv6 router-advertisement gateways through RA silence, re-solicit
    independently of DHCP T1, withdraw on lifetime zero, and parse RIO routes
    with classless safety gates (#11425).
  * Suppress DHCP classless routes covered by same-VRF dynamic RIB or preferred
    routes at FRR apply time; fail closed on incomplete RIB inventory without
    letting dynamic defaults block specific destinations (#11426).
  * Deny unzoned physical ingress before destination-only host-inbound fallback,
    use sdifname for unzoned VRF slaves, and limit zone-scoped admits to
    zone-owned destination addresses (#11409).
  * Reconcile FRR protocol state with HA redundancy-group ownership on primary
    transitions, withdrawing demoted-node peers and restoring sessions on
    promotion (#11415).
  * Burst newly enabled ip-monitoring probes on HA promotion so preferred
    routes follow current path health without waiting for normal test
    intervals (#11414).
  * Repair daemon IPsec SA test fixtures for the shared-bind selector gate:
    give each same-config VPN its own bind so attribution cells stay green
    (#11380).
  * Rotate capped force-probe target windows deterministically so large stale
    neighbor sets reach gateways within bounded ticks (#11407).
  * Apply RFC 7915's size-keyed DF policy to translated NAT64 IPv4 packets and
    fragment eligible outputs to the egress MTU before tunnel encapsulation
    (#11353).
  * Gate planned redundancy-group transfers on routing-table-specific dynamic
    routing evidence, with an explicit per-group degraded-routing override
    (#11377).
  * Suppress management-VRF DHCP classless routes contained by connected
    prefixes by default, and warn when the trust override restores them while
    retaining the non-overridable cluster control/fabric fence (#11383).
  * Reject VPNs sharing a secure-tunnel bind unless their rendered selector
    unions are provably disjoint, preventing cross-VPN SA selection (#11380).
  * Reject exact duplicate AllowedIPs across the merged peers of an
    interface-level WireGuard endpoint, naming the conflicting prefix and
    peers while preserving valid overlapping prefixes (#11381).
  * Fence option-121 routes from overriding connected cluster control/fabric
    prefixes in table 999, regardless of the DHCP trust override (#11362).
  * Select a deterministic per-family management DHCP default and warn when
    competing leases exist, avoiding silent map-order gateway changes (#11363).
  * Reject configured cluster lifelines as tenant routing-instance members and
    quarantine them on tolerant loads so data co-members retain ingress scope;
    diagnose mapped management-class NICs without host-inbound lifeline
    exemption (#11364, #11365).
  * Honor interface > zone > routing-instance context precedence for DNAT and
    static-NAT rule-sets regardless of configuration order (#11351).
  * Guard out-of-normalizer compact `then <head>` leaf forms so routing-instance
    steering survives direct and `apply-groups` compilation (#11354).
  * Require the FBF steering smoke to verify IPv4 and IPv6 forwarding at the
    managed VLAN-80 peer against the resolved ISP-B gateway MAC, reject drop
    and wrong-egress cases, and discover inline/nexthop-id ECMP routes (#11306).
  * Classify child `--fixture` runs as hermetic and keep them out of cluster
    ledger baselines, red-watch selection and coverage (#11343).
  * Order next-table and rib-group leak rules by destination prefix specificity
    across leak kinds so overlapping VRF routes follow longest-prefix match
    in both kernel and userspace dataplanes (#11396).
  * Bind subsequent APT candidate selection to the installer-verified xpf
    channel with a managed Suite/Codename pin; roll it back on failed install
    and remove it on package removal (#11133).
  * Count unconstrained and undefined-routing-instance filter-based-forwarding
    terms as degraded when the kernel mirror fails closed (#11307).
  * Preserve destination-owner host-inbound service admits on VRF netdevs claimed
    by multiple zones, then count unmatched IPv4/IPv6 packets and report the
    ambiguous-ingress transition (#11331).
  * Warn when potentially shadowed DNAT `off` rules use address-book,
    application or cross-rule-set scopes (#11352).
  * Deactivate inet6-only BGP peers for IPv4 so FRR's default cannot open an
    unfiltered IPv4 session (#11374).
  * Initial xpf Debian package (increment A of #1917, subsumes #1923).
    Ships xpfd, xpf-userspace-dp, cli, the day-0 config-drive loader,
    and the systemd units. Binaries install to a dpkg-static staging
    path; live symlinks are created on first install only. The
    in-place upgrade cut-over mechanism is a separate increment.
  * The version field above is a placeholder; `make deb` rewrites it
    from `git describe` before building.
  * Quarantine ambiguous fabric zones away from MAIN routing/session fallback,
    require adjudicated zone stamps for multi-RI redirects, and fail closed on
    unstamped RI-node fabric ingress unless explicit legacy compatibility is
    enabled; reject cross-context zones at strict config commit (#11061).
  * Keep transit forwarding closed when the armed bridge-family barrier
    leg is unsupported; reject malformed SSH authorized_keys entries at
    apply (#10725).
  * Install live-address host-input fences on #1960/#10297 fail-closed
    cold boots, preserving management addresses while blocking data addresses
    until a valid config can be applied (#10732).
  * Install a separate pre-networkd host-input barrier before addresses become
    reachable; admit only loopback/L3/DHCP-client traffic, defer FRR/HA
    ingress, and hand off after enforcement or no-enforcement teardown (#10751).
  * Revoke authoritative userspace persistent NAT leases on clear, refresh the
    display mirror, propagate the operation to the HA peer, and fence stale
    SHOW refreshes and synced-session re-creation. Carry bounded clear fences
    across retained-pool allocator reseeds and same-address pool renames, even
    when no live reservations remain; prune expired keys and convert active-shell
    markers to a finite 60-second horizon when the shell itself is not carried
    (#10784).
  * Register day-0 and Debian maintainer-script regression tests with
    `make selftest` and census both test locations (#10747).
  * Mark subscriber-overrun gaps in CLI flow and packet-drop, gRPC packet-drop,
    and SSE streams, and expose flow-trace drop totals (#10834).
  * Report unknown interface duplex and surface counter/address read failures
    and unmatched interface filters in extensive interface output (#10843).
  * Include responder node identity in chassis-forwarding RPC responses and
    flag divergence between peer response identity and heartbeat belief
    (#10841).
  * Restrict `monitor traffic` to configured interfaces, require an explicit
    host-interface override, and report the requested and resolved capture
    devices (#10845).
  * Show config-sync divergence alarms without active configuration and report
    remote flow-monitor state as unknown (#10846).
  * Label cluster VRRP rows as configured and include per-group detail in
    gRPC cluster status (#10844).
  * Resolve default upgrade rollback targets and version GC from persisted
    committed predecessor history, excluding failed cuts (#10851).
  * Drop NAT64 IPv6 fragments whose Fragment Header names an extension header,
    preserving translated reassembly geometry (#10860).
  * Quarantine super-user event planting received over unauthenticated
    session-sync; preserve it for verified peers (#10870).
  * Preserve scheduler clock-safety and bounded republish retry state across
    config replacement, and retry failed or skipped initial schedule publishes
    (#10873).
  * Send match-all XFRM SA dump requests with the iproute2 address-filter
    attribute, avoiding malformed netlink attribute warnings (#11225).
  * Bound IKE/ESP rekey lifetimes and clamp tolerant DPD timers (#10882).
  * Escape helper errors and recent exception text in monitor terminal output
    (#10904).
  * Refuse MAC-pinned PCI bindings when a known-absent permanent MAC prevents
    identity verification (#10905).
  * Carry the validated fabric zone stamp into parked-fragment retries so
    overlap checks use the encoded zone's routing domain (#10917).
  * Stamp POLICY_DENY records with their evaluating config generation and
    leave stale queued or replayed policy IDs unattributed (#10978).
  * Seed fragment-association sharding, scope admission quotas to
    session identity, and drop associations when their admitting
    session closes (#11058).
  * Return accurate consumed-input counts from sanitizing writers on emit
    errors, permitting retries without duplicating already-emitted lines
    (#10900).
  * Complete factory-reset image-seal cleanup for regenerable device identity,
    managed service state, logs, and DHCP leases; refuse erasure while DDNS or
    IPsec teardown authority remains unresolved (#10769).
  * Prevent peer-echoed idle persistent-NAT leases, defer imported-lease
    promotion until successful local flow completion, restore full lease
    metadata after strict mirror refusal, and keep rollback safe across
    concurrent synced joins. Clamp skewed peer lifetimes at decode boundaries
    and imported lifetimes to the local timeout/schema ceiling (#10789).
  * Update same-key MASTER VIP changes in place; normalize address spelling,
    fence GARP/NA follow-ups before withdrawal, retain unannounced survivors,
    and bound send-lock scope to one VIP at a time (#10780).
  * Bind multi-zone snapshot authorization to the selected peer connection;
    keep stale-auth reports from re-arming after capable-peer convergence,
    make deferral reports and clears attempt-fresh across peer epochs and
    capability changes, and clear superseded alarms only after current active
    config succeeds; preserve local convergence after peer-only push failures
    (#10782).
  * Throttle REST authentication failures per source and account, harden SSH
    password login, and hash configured API-auth secrets (#10825).
  * Scope API-auth identities by login class and UTC expiry, require HTTPS for
    credentials, and migrate persisted credentials to bcrypt verifiers (#10826).
  * Redact named API-key `secret` values in REST config output and diagnostics,
    and hash API credentials received via peer config sync before persistence
    (#10826).
  * Throttle Basic and API-key verification, migrate credentials across active,
    rollback, rescue, and exported configs, and purge affected snapshots only
    from the xpf-owned local archive (#10825).
  * Include named API keys in local and remote `show system services` counts
    (#10826).
  * Flush box-oriented host-inbound conntrack entries and guard denied TCP/UDP
    replies before established accepts; disable TCP loose pickup at boot/runtime
    (#10752/#10764).
  * Scope stale host-input guards by ingress zone with trusted-reinject
    fallback, reassert verified TCP loose pickup disablement, and harden
    packet proof with HIGH exempt-UDP residual (#10752/#10764).
  * Preserve exact conntrack tuples through host-inbound tightening warning
    projection, attributing evidence only to policy transitions that removed
    that tuple's admission (#11493).
  * Resolve routing-instance ownership by Linux device identity, reject
    alias/tunnel dual claims, and quarantine ambiguous memberships on tolerant
    loads with an apply alarm and alertable metric (#11060).
  * Scope rib-group return paths to peer prefixes and peer tables so unrelated
    VRF misses cannot fall through to main; warn when next-table/PBR targets
    may lack a return route (#11062/#11320).
  * Warn about and exclude static routes without a forwarding disposition, so
    they cannot shadow an installable less-specific route in the helper FIB
    (#11327).
  * Defer never-seen HA absence confirmation while connected session-sync
    receive proof is fresh; preserve startup grace and readiness gates (#11566).
  * Align userspace-dp session-sync regression fixtures with the ingress
    identity trailer, preserve JSON/binary identity parity, and keep the
    policy-list acknowledgement plus debug timing gates robust under runner
    contention (#11546).
  * Reject undeclared fields in named API-auth credentials and validate
    API-auth class references; reconcile the schema-census inventories
    (#11544).
  * Reject multiple default-policy choices with an accurate diagnostic and
    fail tolerant loads closed instead of compiling first-wins permit (#11367).
  * Bump the helper FIB generation after learned-route republish and retain
    retry state when invalidation fails (#11565).
  * Fail closed when an embedded ICMP quote's translated NAT tuple is ambiguous
    across routing domains, while retaining off-path reversal for unique flows
    (#11298).
  * Index local and shared tuple identities for delayed session-close checks,
    preserving scoped-incarnation teardown while avoiding slab and shared-map
    scans under the shared-session mutex (#11299).
  * Route oversized same-binding flow-cache hits through pending-forward so
    normal egress MTU, PTB, and TCP-segmentation handling is preserved (#11376).

  * Resolve native-fragment protocol 255 from the declared IP header before
    filter, PBR, and CoS matching; unresolved sentinels no longer wildcard
    protocol-constrained terms (#11338).

  * Expire DHCPv4/v6 stateful leases at their absolute deadline after failed
    T1/T2 renewal and reacquisition. Remove stale addresses and delegated
    prefixes, retain stateless DHCPv6 options across failed refreshes, and
    notify dependent route recompilation (#11382).
  * Preserve Linux RTAX_MTU on imported routes through the v38 FIB snapshot,
    applying selected-route limits to plain forwarding, tunnel budgets, TCP
    segmentation, and PMTU signaling (#11411).
  * Refresh learned-route FIBs from coalesced kernel route events, and retry
    unresolved FIB-generation bumps without publishing once per event (#11565).
  * Preflight userspace snapshots before host-mutating compiler phases, then
    retain and report accepted snapshot generations when post-publish
    reconciliation fails (#11080).
  * Keep selector-bearing ip rules out of destination-only FIB leaks, constrain
    explicit next hops to their route's routing instance, and scope/recheck
    transit martians on neighbor replay and final transmit (#11074).
